  --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary

- Adds `CondenseAndMarkFullyCondensed` called from the stop hook — condenses session data to `entire/checkpoints/v1` immediately when the agent stops and marks `FullyCondensed=true`
- PostCommit skips `FullyCondensed+ENDED` sessions at the top of the loop, paying only a cheap JSON load instead of shadow-branch tree traversal
- Drops the shadow-tree session-discovery approach (separate indexing branch) — not needed since the eager-condense skip is sufficient

## Why not shadow-tree indexing?
With eager condense + the `isFullyCondensedEnded` skip, the expensive `postCommitProcessSession` is bypassed entirely. The only remaining cost is `listAllSessionStates` (cheap git ref lookups, <1ms each). Shadow-tree indexing added ENDED carry-forward complexity without proportional gain.

